\label{def:SGAC}
	We say that the joint distribution $\mathbf P\!_n$ of the random 
	vectors $\boldsymbol X_1,\ldots,\boldsymbol X_n\in\mathbb{R}^p$ belongs to
	the sub-Gaussian model with adversarial contamination
	with mean $\boldsymbol\mu^*$, covariance matrix $\boldsymbol\Sigma$ and 
	contamination rate $\varepsilon$, if there are independent
	random vectors $\boldsymbol\xi_i\sim SG_p(\tau)$ such that 
	\begin{align}
	    \Big|\Big\{i:=1,\ldots,n:\boldsymbol X_i \neq \boldsymbol\mu^*+ \boldsymbol\Sigma^{1/2}
	    \boldsymbol\xi_i\Big\}\Big|\le \varepsilon n.
	\end{align}
	We then write $\mathbf P\!_n\in \textup{SGAC}(\boldsymbol\mu^*,\boldsymbol\Sigma, 
	\varepsilon)$.

